  "generated_text": "1. **Understanding the Composition of Functions:**\n   We are given $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$. This means $f(x) = q(p(r(x)))$.\n\n2. **Finding the Inverse of the Composition:**\n   To find $f^{-1}$, we need to reverse the steps of $f$. This means we first apply the inverse of $q$, then the inverse of $p$, and finally the inverse of $r$. Thus, $f^{-1}(x) = r^{-1}(p^{-1}(q^{-1}(x)))$.\n\n3. **Expressing the Inverse Function:**\n   The correct expression for $f^{-1}$ is $r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}$.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   The correct expression for $f^{-1}$ is $r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}$, which corresponds to option C.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
  "grade": {
